<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA C.BANK REFINANCING FALLS TO 61 BLN LEVS.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA C.BANK REFINANCING FALLS TO 61 BLN LEVS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian National Bank's (BNB)</p>
<p>refinancing to commercial banks stood at 61.044 billion levs on</p>
<p>November 15, down from 62.044 billion levs on November 8, BNB</p>
<p>preliminary figures showed.</p>
<p>The fall was due to a decrease in Lombard loans by one</p>
<p>billion levs in the week to November 15, figures showed.</p>
<p>  BNB refinancing, mln levs     NOV 15     NOV 8    OCT 25</p>
<p>  Uncollaterlised deposits	 8,616     8,616     8,616</p>
<p>  Lombard loans			4,858     5,858     5,858</p>
<p>  Discount loans			   0	   0	   0</p>
<p>  Overdraft				107	 107	 107</p>
<p>  Overdue loans and deposits    47,463    47,463    47,463</p>
<p>  Total loans and deposits	61,044    62,044    63,061</p>
<p>  BNB treasury porfolio	   85,096    75,975    80,337</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
